"""Provider-routing regression tests for deep_research/config.py.

Both tables below were captured from the PRE-refactor ``model_required_keys``
and ``get_model`` (duplicated substring chains) by running the original module
with recording stubs; they are literals, never computed from the code under
test, and are the contract the single ``_PROVIDERS`` table must keep.

REQUIRED_KEYS: model name -> {route_via_openrouter: model_required_keys result}.

CASES: one row per scenario ``(model, env_keys_set, get_model_kwargs,
module ROUTE_VIA_OPENROUTER, expected)``. Only ``env_keys_set`` are present in
the environment (fake values ``"k-<ENV_NAME>"``, so ``api_key`` also shows WHICH
variable a branch read). ``expected`` is the full call recorded by the stub
clients: ``(tag, positional args, keyword args, warning log messages)`` where
tag is ChatOpenAI / ChatDeepSeek / init_chat_model, or ``("ERR", exception type
name, message)``. No network calls and no real keys are used.
"""
